Spec: Owner-started Android foreground gateway

Purpose:
  Hold business runtime lifetime under explicit owner control without permitting SDKs to start or stop it.

Owns:
  ./GatewayService.java

Must:
  Remain unexported, use connected-device foreground type and provide a private immutable stop action.
  Separate UI closure from gateway stop, make stop suppress restart and restore only previously owner-enabled runtime after eligible system restart.
  Load a valid existing Keystore identity before networking and expose a fixed stopped state on setup failure.

  Perform enrollment validation and server handshake on a bounded background worker, publish only the current startup generation and close any late result after owner stop.
  A present invalid server configuration stops startup with a fixed error; it never starts the unauthenticated-authority preview.

  Serialize boot journal recovery with final startup-generation publication so an obsolete startup cannot close a newer runtime's opens.

  Queue owner start/stop actions through the unexported service rather than stopping an undelivered foreground start; each start command satisfies foreground registration before applying owner state.
  A destroyed superseded service instance must not stop or unpublish a newer instance.
